---
// THE AUDIT TRAIL. Each section is one question a Salesforce developer would ask, the artifact
// that answers it, and the command that reproduces it.
//
// The page used to be a pile of artifacts with no voice saying what question each one answered,
// which is how it came to confuse its own author. Three blocks of methodology prose could not
// state their question in one line and moved to /docs/measurement.
//
// Keep the shape: question, artifact, reproduce. A section that needs a paragraph to justify
// itself is a docs page wearing a receipt's clothes.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import data from '../data/capabilities.json';

const title = 'Receipts — every number, and the command that produced it';
const description =
  'Every number on fidelic.dev, the command that produced it, and the denominator it is counted against.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="back"><a href="/capabilities">← What Fidelic can run</a></p>
    <h1>Receipts</h1>

    <p>
      Every figure here is produced by running something, and each block names what.
    </p>

    <h2>What does it print when I point it at a real org?</h2>
    <div class="terminal" role="img" aria-label="Terminal transcript: the sfapex analyzer classifies the Nonprofit Success Pack's 26 triggers at load time as 7 EXECUTE and 19 UNRESOLVED; the emulator then boots that org in 14.1 seconds and, with failure injection enabled, a PATCH returns HTTP 400 with an UNABLE_TO_LOCK_ROW error array.">
      <pre><span class="dim"># what will run, before running it</span>
<span class="cmd">docker run --rm -v ./npsp/force-app:/mdapi:ro --entrypoint /sfapex fidelic/emulator coverage /mdapi</span>
COVERAGE
  parsed:   1061 files (0 with ERROR nodes, 0 error nodes total)
  found:    26 trigger(s), 1503 class(es)

RUNG B LADDER @ C1 + C2 families &#123;async, callout, crypto, database, recorded-effect, schema, schema-permission, settings&#125; <span class="dim">(load-time classification)</span>: EXECUTE=7  HOOKS=0  UNRESOLVED=19  RECORDED-ONLY=0  (SIMULATED=1)
  <span class="ok">EXECUTE</span>     TDTM_DataImportBatch  [Provisional: schema: describe labels derived where the metadata carries none; DisplayType modeled as its enum name; == identity on describe results Provisional (SCHEMA-DESIGN §7)]
  <span class="sim">EXECUTE*</span>    TDTM_FormTemplate  (SIMULATED: settings: Gift_Entry_Settings__c.getInstance — Custom Setting read at C2; settings: Gift_Entry_Settings__c.getOrgDefaults — Custom Setting read at C2)  [Provisional: schema: describe labels derived where the metadata carries none; DisplayType modeled as its enum name; == identity on describe results Provisional (SCHEMA-DESIGN §7)]
  <span class="bad">UNRESOLVED</span>  TDTM_HouseholdObject  (min tier C3; blocked by dispatch: interface Evaluator [C3])

<span class="dim"># now boot it, with the row-lock fault armed</span>
<span class="cmd">docker run -p 8080:8080 -v ./npsp/force-app:/mdapi:ro -e SFEMU_FAULT_LOCK_ON_UPDATE=true fidelic/emulator --apex-src /mdapi</span>
sfemu: apexexec ON — 26 triggers loaded from "/mdapi", 7 EXECUTE-classified
sfemu … listening on :8080 (store: sqlite ":memory:", client-secret: false, metadata: "/mdapi", hooks-file: "")
<span class="dim"># 14.1s to listening — NPSP, 26 triggers / 1,503 classes, 3-vCPU cloud VM</span>

<span class="cmd">curl -sX PATCH localhost:8080/services/data/v62.0/sobjects/Account/001000000000038AAA \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '&#123;"Rating":"Hot"&#125;'</span>
<span class="bad">HTTP 400</span>
<span class="bad">[&#123;"message":"unable to obtain exclusive access to this record or 1 records",</span>
<span class="bad">  "errorCode":"UNABLE_TO_LOCK_ROW","fields":[]&#125;]</span></pre>
    </div>
    <p class="src">
      Reproduce: the three commands are in the block, run against
      <a href="https://github.com/SalesforceFoundation/NPSP">NPSP</a> @ 19646faa
      (<code>force-app</code>) on <code>fidelic/emulator:4ea9d49</code>. Three of the 26 trigger
      rows are shown.
    </p>

    <h2>Does the emulator match Salesforce behaviour?</h2>
    <p class="figure">{data.conformance.passed} of {data.conformance.total} conformance tests pass.</p>
    <p class="denom"><strong>Denominator:</strong> {data.conformance.denominator}</p>
    <p class="src">Reproduce: <code>{data.conformance.command}</code></p>

    <h2>Which of my org's triggers will actually run?</h2>
    <p class="figure">
      {data.coverage.executePairs} of {data.coverage.pairs} trigger-context pairs classify
      EXECUTE, across {data.coverage.executeTriggers} of {data.coverage.triggers} triggers.
      That is {data.coverage.percent}%.
    </p>
    <p class="denom"><strong>Denominator:</strong> {data.coverage.denominator}</p>
    <p class="src">Reproduce: <code>{data.coverage.command}</code> against {data.coverage.corpus}</p>

    <h2>Is that number just true of the org you picked?</h2>
    <p class="figure">
      142 of 554 trigger-context pairs classify EXECUTE across five public Salesforce
      codebases — 23 of their 82 triggers.
    </p>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Codebase</th><th>Triggers</th><th>EXECUTE</th><th>UNRESOLVED</th><th>Pairs</th><th>%</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/SalesforceFoundation/Cumulus">NPSP</a> <code>19646faa</code></td>
              <td>26</td><td>8</td><td>18</td><td>51/177</td><td>28%</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/SalesforceFoundation/EDA">EDA</a> <code>b311845</code></td>
              <td>37</td><td>11</td><td>26</td><td>77/259</td><td>29%</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/SFDO-Community/declarative-lookup-rollup-summaries">DLRS</a> <code>8e43f01</code></td>
              <td>14</td><td>0</td><td>14</td><td>0/97</td><td>0%</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/trailheadapps/apex-recipes">apex-recipes</a> <code>87c1c9b</code></td>
              <td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>2/9</td><td>22%</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="https://github.com/financialforcedev/fflib-apex-common-samplecode">fflib-samplecode</a> <code>4657d63</code></td>
              <td>2</td><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>12/12</td><td>100%</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="denom"><strong>Denominator:</strong> every trigger-context pair declared by every
      trigger in the checked-out source, at the commit named beside each codebase. DLRS reads 0%
      because five separate blockers hit all 14 of its triggers, four of them things a public
      checkout does not carry: managed-package references and custom objects whose metadata was
      never retrieved.</p>
    <p class="src">Reproduce, per codebase: <code>docker run --rm -v "$PWD/force-app":/mdapi:ro --entrypoint /sfapex fidelic/emulator coverage /mdapi</code></p>

    <h2 id="vocabulary">What do EXECUTE, SIMULATED and UNRESOLVED mean?</h2>
    <dl class="vocab">
      <dt><span class="v v-exec">EXECUTE</span></dt>
      <dd>No blocker was found in the reachable code, so the interpreter will attempt your real Apex.</dd>
      <dt><span class="v v-sim">SIMULATED</span></dt>
      <dd>Your code runs. One or more named things were modelled instead of performed, and each one is named.</dd>
      <dt><span class="v v-prov">Provisional</span></dt>
      <dd>The behaviour is faithful. The response <em>envelope</em> has not yet been confirmed
      against a real org. A capability can carry this label and SIMULATED at the same time.</dd>
      <dt><span class="v v-ref">UNRESOLVED</span></dt>
      <dd>Declined by name, with the file and line that caused it.</dd>
      <dt><span class="v v-rec">RECORDED-ONLY</span></dt>
      <dd>The code could run, but the event that starts it cannot happen locally: a
      platform-event subscriber, for instance.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="src">Reproduce: your own coverage report prints these same words.</p>

    <h2>Which Apex features are supported, one at a time?</h2>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Family</th><th>What it covers</th><th>Verdict</th><th>Caveat</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {data.capabilities.map((c) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{c.family}</code></td>
              <td>{c.note}</td>
              <td>
                <span class={c.verdict === 'EXECUTE' ? 'v v-exec' : 'v v-ref'}>{c.verdict}</span>
              </td>
              <td>
                {c.simulated && <div class="caveat"><span class="v v-sim">SIMULATED</span> {c.simulationNote}</div>}
                {c.provisional && <div class="caveat"><span class="v v-prov">Provisional</span> {c.provisional}</div>}
                {!c.simulated && !c.provisional && <span class="none">—</span>}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="src">Reproduce: <code>{data.capabilitiesCommand}</code></p>

    <h2>Do these numbers match the binary I would download?</h2>
    <p class="stamp">
      Generated {data.generated} from build <code>{data.build}</code>, against image
      <code>{data.imageRef}</code>, which reports <code>{data.imageVersion}</code>. Shipped
      tier: <code>{data.shippedTier}</code>.
    </p>
    <p class="src">Reproduce: <code>docker run --rm {data.imageRef} version</code></p>

    <h2>How do I run this against my own org?</h2>
    <pre><code>docker run --rm -v "$PWD/mdapi":/mdapi:ro \
  --entrypoint /sfapex fidelic/emulator coverage --report /mdapi</code></pre>
    <p class="src">
      How these figures are built: <a href="/docs/measurement">how the numbers are measured</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .stamp{font-size:.85rem;color:#57606a;background:#f6f8fa;border-left:3px solid #89b4fa;
    padding:.6rem .85rem;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0}
  .src{font-size:.85rem;color:#57606a;margin-bottom:.4rem}
  .figure{font-size:1.05rem;margin:.2rem 0 .5rem}
  .denom{font-size:.85rem;color:#24292f;background:#f6f8fa;padding:.6rem .85rem;border-radius:4px}
  .fine{font-size:.9rem;color:#57606a}
  .tablewrap{overflow-x:auto}
  table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.9rem;margin:.5rem 0 1.5rem}
  th,td{text-align:left;padding:.45rem .6rem;border-bottom:1px solid #d0d7de;vertical-align:top}
  th{font-size:.8rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.03em;color:#57606a}
  .v{display:inline-block;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;font-size:.72rem;
    padding:.08rem .4rem;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;margin-right:.25rem}
  .v-exec{background:#dafbe1;color:#0a5a2a}
  .v-sim{background:#fff4d6;color:#7a5200}
  .v-prov{background:#e7e9ff;color:#33389a}
  .v-ref{background:#ffe9ec;color:#8b1d2c}
  .v-rec{background:#eef1f4;color:#44506b}
  .caveat{font-size:.82rem;color:#57606a;margin-bottom:.3rem}
  .caveat:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
  .none{color:#8c959f}
  .vocab dt{margin-top:.6rem}
  .vocab dd{margin:.15rem 0 .4rem 0;font-size:.92rem}
  @media (max-width:640px){ table{font-size:.82rem} }
</style>
